title: Authorizations › New case › Workflow › Default process and equal matches
route: /authorizations/new/:draftId (the Workflow line under the stepper)
intro: When no published workflow fits the case, New case uses a clearly labelled default process for the request type and invents no payer rule. When two published workflows are equally specific, nothing is picked silently: the line names both, the default is used, and a person chooses in a small side panel. The choice is written to the case's history with who made it.
dir: TD
also: The default is illustrative. It is not payer policy and it never claims a payer rule. The wording of the default is the same for each request type: 'Default process for a concurrent review. No payer workflow matches. Illustrative, not payer policy.'
---
start s1 "The case's payer, level of care and Authorization type are known"
process p1 "The published workflows are matched"
decision d1 "What did the match find?"

group gNone "Nothing matches"
  store n1 "The labelled default for the request type is stored on the draft\n'Default process for a concurrent review'"
  store n2 "History: 'Default workflow applied: Default process for a concurrent review'\nDetail: the match explanation"
  screen n3 "Workflow line\n'Workflow: Default process for a concurrent review'\nPill 'Illustrative default'\nNo version or payer after the name"
  click n4 "Hover over the info icon"
  overlay n5 "'Default process for a concurrent review. No payer workflow matches. Illustrative, not payer policy.'"
endgroup

group gConf "Two workflows are equally specific"
  store c1 "The default is stored on the draft for now"
  screen c2 "Workflow line\n'Workflow: Default process for a ... Illustrative default'\nIn amber: '<Workflow A> and <Workflow B> match equally. The default is used until you choose.'\nButton 'Choose a workflow'"
  click c3 "Click 'Choose a workflow'"
  overlay c4 "Side panel 'Choose a workflow'\nOne radio choice per workflow: name, version, request type, services, effective date, why it matched"
  input c5 "Pick one"
  click c6 "Click 'Use this workflow'"
  click c7 "Click 'Keep the default for now', press Escape, or click outside"
  process c8 "The panel closes\nThe default stays"
  store c9 "The choice is stored on the case with the names it was chosen among\nThe workflow replaces the default (it is pinned once the workflow has run past Intake)"
  store c10 "History: 'Workflow chosen: Initial Authorization, Residential SUD v3 (Initial Authorization, IOP matched equally)'\nDetail: who chose and why they matched"
  toast c11 "'Workflow applied'\n'Initial Authorization, Residential SUD, version 3 is what this case follows now.'"
endgroup

decision d2 "Does the case change so the same two no longer compete?"
process p2 "The choice no longer holds\nA fresh match is made (before the workflow has run past Intake), or offered for review (after)"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Workflow › Match and pin the payer workflow"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Workflow › The case changed after the workflow started"
end e1 "The case follows the workflow a person chose"
end e2 "The case follows the default, clearly labelled"

s1 --> p1 --> d1
d1 -->|No match| n1 --> n2 --> n3 --> e2
n3 --> n4 --> n5
d1 -->|Equal matches| c1 --> c2 --> c3 --> c4 --> c5 --> c6 --> c9 --> c10 --> c11 --> e1
c4 --> c7 --> c8 --> e2
d1 -->|One best match| g1
c11 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| p2 --> g2
d2 -->|No| e1
